<!--
  AWS S3 wodle configuration — pulls CloudTrail logs from S3 into Wazuh.
  Insert this block inside <ossec_config>...</ossec_config> in:
    /var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf

  Notes / gotchas discovered while building this (see README "Challenges &
  Lessons Learned" for full detail):

  1. Do NOT add a <path> tag for a bucket of type="cloudtrail" — Wazuh's
     CloudTrail parser already auto-prepends "AWSLogs/" internally. Adding
     an explicit <path>AWSLogs</path> causes a duplicated prefix
     ("AWSLogs/AWSLogs/") and the module silently finds zero logs.

  2. The <aws_profile> value below must exactly match a profile name in
     the AWS credentials file used by the wazuh service account
     (typically /var/ossec/.aws/credentials on Debian/Ubuntu installs).

  3. If wazuh-manager runs under systemd, boto3 may fail to locate that
     credentials file with "The config profile could not be found" even
     when the file is present and correctly permissioned — systemd
     services do not always inherit $HOME the way an interactive shell
     session does. Fix via a systemd override setting
     Environment="HOME=/var/ossec" (or wherever your wazuh user's home
     directory actually is — confirm with: grep wazuh /etc/passwd).

  4. If wazuh-analysisd logs "ERROR: Too many fields for JSON decoder",
     raise analysisd.decoder_order_size (default 256, max 1024) in
     /var/ossec/etc/local_internal_options.conf. This is a known,
     documented limitation with large/nested CloudTrail events
     (e.g. IAM policy documents in requestParameters) and is not
     guaranteed to fully eliminate the error even at the maximum value.
-->
<wodle name="aws-s3">
  <disabled>no</disabled>
  <interval>10m</interval>
  <run_on_start>yes</run_on_start>
  <skip_on_error>no</skip_on_error>
  <bucket type="cloudtrail">
    <name>YOUR-CLOUDTRAIL-BUCKET-NAME</name>
    <aws_profile>wazuh-cloudtrail</aws_profile>
  </bucket>
</wodle>
